WEBVTT

NOTE
Disc 2 - Scene 29h: Time Compression Begins
Duration: ~26 seconds
Reality Warping and Temporal Distortion
For blind and low-vision players using screen readers

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
The world around the party begins to warp and twist. The crystalline walls of the Lunatic 
Pandora fracture and fragment, creating jagged, impossible angles. Space itself seems to 
fold in directions that defy normal geometry.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
The sky fractures into a thousand geometric patterns — triangles, hexagons, and impossible 
shapes that have no names. Colors splinter across the sky like cracks in glass. Blues, 
purples, and sickly greens intermix with flashes of white light.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
Landscapes from different time periods begin to bleed into one another. A futuristic cityscape 
with towering chrome buildings overlays itself with a medieval castle of stone and aged wood. 
The two environments merge impossibly, creating a surreal hybrid landscape.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.000
A desert of golden sand suddenly gives way to a churning ocean. Waves crash where dunes once 
stood. Tropical islands fade in and out of reality, existing and ceasing to exist in 
successive moments. Desert cacti stand beside snow-capped mountains.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.000
The colors shift and swirl in nauseating patterns. Warm oranges become cool blues in an 
instant. Vibrant greens fade to sickly grays and back again. The party's surroundings seem 
to lose all stability.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.000
The ground beneath the party's feet becomes unstable. It shifts from solid stone to sand to 
water and back again in rapid succession. Gravity seems to waver. The entire world is folding 
in on itself.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.000
The party staggers and struggles to remain upright. Disorientation is written across their 
faces. They struggle to maintain their sense of self, their identities fragmenting as time 
collapses around them.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:26.000
Time Compression intensifies. Multiple moments exist simultaneously. The past, present, and 
future occupy the same space. The fundamental order of existence is unraveling before their 
eyes.
